m #545&#x27;s passes rather than edited there because the text is the timer campaign&#x27;s: &#x27;EVERY REAL ROW IN THIS FILE COMPARES NUMBERS&#x27; (E2, E3, F1 and G1 compare strings); the fbclearread paragraph in the present tense (&#x27;case TIMER_1_CLEAR: carries NO writeflag test&#x27;) after #474 guarded it; and &#x27;a DISABLED timer can never hold a pending interrupt&#x27; (also in gate_offline.sh) -- the timer callbacks count pending ticks without testing TIMER_ENABLE, and disabling does not remove the registered timer: a product question for the timer campaign as well as a records one.</span><span class="tip">records: three pre-existing false sentences in regress/diff_footbridge.c and regress/gate_offline.sh, filed from #545&#x27;s passes rather than edited there because the text is the timer campaign&#x27;s: &#x27;EVERY REAL ROW IN THIS FILE COMPARES NUMBERS&#x27; (E2, E3, F1 and G1 compare strings); the fbclearread paragraph in the present tense (&#x27;case TIMER_1_CLEAR: carries NO writeflag test&#x27;) after #474 guarded it; and &#x27;a DISABLED timer can never hold a pending interrupt&#x27; (also in gate_offline.sh) -- the timer callbacks count pending ticks without testing TIMER_ENABLE, and disabling does not remove the registered timer: a product question for the timer campaign as well as a records one.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></t