rid">fbctrlcmdkill</span><span class="ttl">dev_fbctrl.c: any command other than 0-2 ends the emulator process, including the documented but unimplemented FILL and COPY -- guest-reachable through one DATA write at selector 0</span><span class="tip">dev_fbctrl.c: any command other than 0-2 ends the emulator process, including the documented but unimplemented FILL and COPY -- guest-reachable through one DATA write at selector 0 — note: [2026-10-19 06:3x, IN WORK -- working-tree progress note] F2 ANSWERED (regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/pass2_20261018/f2/F2_DISPOSITIONS.md): GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7 and GLM 5.3 all SHIP WITH CHANGES (Fable 5.1 walled, held); they converge on WIDTH x BOUND EDGE and the latch&#x27;s persistence.  Kill table 3a measured seven escapes of the 99-row v2 (killtable3a_20261019/); probe v3 (106 rows) closed them, and kill table 3 re-ran all 32 mutants on it: every one red, every prediction held (killtable3_20261019/).  Reading the arm for the REST of the width class found more open cells -- a bound relaxed in one (width, latch) cell restores the host kill -- so probe v4 (123 rows) closes the class in ONE diff from an explicit enumeration (killtable4_20261019/PRETABLE_ADDENDUM_t4.out, written before v4 ran); kill table 4 is running.  Then: v4 and its gate block into the tree, one real gate-16 run each way, the repair&#x27;s own pass, Astra&#x27;s confirm, commit A (the census) and #567.  ||  [2026-10-19 05:5x, IN WORK -- working-tree progress note] The battery passed 16/16 with #567 in the tree (gate 16 ran its block: 95/95).  Pass 2 (GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7, GLM 5.3; Fable walled, held): all three SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Kill table 2a measured the unbuilt mutants they named on the 95-row probe -- three escaped (a read falling into the store branch, every non-word access refused, wide values passing once the latch is set) -- so the probe became v2, 99 rows, and gate 16 checks every row by name; kill table 2 re-ran all 25 mutants on v2: every one red (regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/killtable2a_20261019/, killtable2_20261019/).  A 16-byte vector store (testppc stvx) reaching the device as its low 64 bits is disclosed and to be filed (fbctrlvec128).  The adjudication pass (F2) is out to Astra, Grok and GLM; the census repair lands first as its own commit.  ||  [2026-10-18 23:2x, IN WORK -- working-tree progress note] Kill table 1 (21:34-21:42) and its addendum table 1b (23:13-23:17) are DONE: sixteen mutants, every one red, both null media red (15/95, CONTROL=FAILED), and every table-1b prediction held row for row (regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/killtable1_20261018/, killtable1b_20261018/).  The fix, the 95-row probe and its gate 16 block are in the working tree; the shipped probe scores 36/95 on HEAD and 95/95 on the fix (pass2_20261018/legs/).  The battery was re-triggered at 23:19 with them in it; pass 2, F2, the confirm and the commit follow it.  ||  [2026-10-18 21:4x, IN WORK -- working-tree progress note] The 18:00 weekly battery DIED at ~18:13 (the laptop changed power source and entered Modern Standby; gate 3 of 16, no verdict), so the code work did not wait for a finished battery.  Kill table 1 has been running in the scratch clone /tmp/gx567 since 21:34: 11 mutants plus 2 null media, every prediction written in PRETABLE.out beforehand.  The battery is re-triggered after it (~22:05 -&gt; ~02:00); pass 2, F2, the confirm and the commit come after that.  ||  [2026-10-18 17:32, IN WORK -- working-tree progress note] PRETABLE.out written 17:30:58, before any kill table; it grew the draft detector to 95 rows (byte and halfword refusals: the gate never tests len).  Measured on that instrument: PRE-FIX 36/95 -- exactly its prediction -- and the draft fix 95/95 (regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/draft_20261018/).  Kill table, pass 2, F2, confirm and commit after the weekly battery (~22:15).  ||  [2026-10-18 17:29, IN WORK -- working-tree progress note] Draft fix (round #567) and an 83-row draft detector MEASURED in scratch clones, one frozen instrument: PRE-FIX (HEAD&#x27;s binary) 34/83 -- six command classes kill the host and the three wide aliases of accepted commands silently run NOP / SET_RESOLUTION / GET_RESOLUTION; POST-FIX 83/83; the witness 2/12 -&gt; 12/12 (regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/draft_20261018/).  Not yet in the tree: the PRETABLE check, the kill table, pass 2 on the diff, F2 and Astra&#x27;s confirm come after the weekly battery (18:00 -&gt; ~22:15).  ||  [2026-10-18 17:2x, IN WORK -- working-tree progress note] Pass 1 ADJUDICATED (regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/pass1_20261018/ADJUDICATION_p1.md): GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7 and GLM 5.3 all chose member 3 -- refuse every full 64-bit DATA value other than 0, 1 and 2 at COMMAND BEFORE the store, leave COMMAND unchanged, one new warned_cmd latch and one (once) announce naming the full value; a new gated probe; fbctrloffkill stays its own row (2-1).  Fable 5.1 walled (held).  Code waits for the weekly battery (18:00 -&gt; ~22:15).  ||  [2026-10-18 17:1x, IN WORK -- working-tree progress note, not yet committed] Test-first witness MEASURED at rung 3 on HEAD&#x27;s binary (unmodified -E testmips): a DATA write of command 3 (FILL), 4 (COPY), 5, -1 or sd 0x100000003 (truncated to 3 in the int port cell) each end the host with exit 1; controls OK (liveness 0x2a; GET_RESOLUTION zeroes X1); FBCMDW_RESULT=2/12 (regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/pass1_20261018/WITNESS_headbin.out).  Design pass 1 fired 17:14 (GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7, GLM 5.3; Fable tried once).  The round&#x27;s code work waits for the 2026-10-18 weekly battery to finish (~22:15).</span></span><span class="state st-in work">in work</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #549&#x27;s review -- the finding, its seats and its ev