 HEAD observes testmips&#x27;s &gt;256 MB mirror/high mapping (#120&#x27;s &quot;regression-gated&quot; has no carrier; every `-M` under regress/ is 32 or 64) || gberesizezero -- GBE keeps a rejected VCMAP/HCMAP dimension in xres/yres and reads it back through negative shifts || vgacursoronly -- VGA headless console: the OB-16 guard returns before the cursor-only tick can reposition the terminal cursor || pxdmatail -- PX COPYSPANS decodes span records past the bytes the bounded SRAM copy filled || gifputcharovf -- ps2_gif putchar: (24 + y*xsize)*4 overflows int before #108&#x27;s bound; residual of the RESOLVED OB-28 || pxfilladd -- PX fill: int32_t lw + 1 overflows at INT32_MAX before the row loop || lunaintshift -- luna88k: signed 1 &lt;&lt; 31 in the INT_ST_MASK read loop and the line-6 assert/deassert, and highestCurrentStatus &lt;&lt; 29 for levels 4-6 || kn02banameshift -- kn02ba: 1 &lt;&lt; i for i == 31 in the interrupt-name snprintf, the sibling #24 cast at :192 did not || macesignedshift -- MACE assert/deassert compute 1 &lt;&lt; line in int; line 31 is registered and undefined || autodevregorder -- diff_autodev_gen.sh&#x27;s ordered rows compare PROTOTYPE lines; the registration loops are a separate scrape no row observes || lunad3diag -- no row observes luna_intmask_probe.py&#x27;s D3 diagnostic (its &quot;kills a narrowed guard&quot; sentence is ambiguous, not false) || fdcdiagrows -- CHANGELOG #20522&#x27;s &quot;asserted rather than assumed&quot; fdc measurement has no committed carrier || fileloaderrows -- (no ECOFF/Mach-O/SREC/Android corpus row; gate_upstream.sh says so itself) || ascaccountrows -- (no committed row asserts NCR_TCL/NCR_TCM/NCRSTAT_TC) || cuemapgap -- (#127&#x27;s &quot;each regression-gated&quot; CUE claims have no carrier; diff_diskimage_io.c routes reads away from the CUE path) || modeselectrow -- (no diff_diskimage_*.c row issues opcode 0x15) || scsicaprow -- (diff_diskimage_parse.c asserts the PARSER&#x27;s count, never READ CA