read the output || findaddrwrap -- Debugger memory search can wrap its scan address into low addresses || findcountovf -- Debugger search counts matches and unreadable chunks in unbounded signed ints || dbgignorow -- No committed row observes breakpoint ignore-count stops || mipsbpnormrow -- No committed row observes MIPS breakpoint sign-extension of an unextended address || subsysbprow -- No committed row arms a subsystem breakpoint and observes debugger entry || dbglisterow -- No committed row observes the global break-on-ERROR listing after one subsystem is cleared || stepcallfocus -- Changing machine focus leaves step-call running cached untraced handlers || netipurgptr -- TCP reply checksum covers an urgent pointer the reply never stores || netipseqarith -- TCP sequence difference is a signed subtraction before the mismatch reject || netipbcastmask -- Broadcast mask shifts a signed 1 by an accepted prefix || arcseekshift -- ARC Seek retains a signed byte-decoding shift || arcstdinlimit -- ARC stdin Read overflows its signed loop counter at length 2147483647 || irqcmaskshift -- IRQ mask and unmask writes still use a signed 1 shifted by the guest selector || isopathptr -- ISO path-table checks form pointers beyond one-past || shdmteupper -- OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:8691-8694 at db8b1a33 -- the SH DMAC interrupt loop stops at DMAE (0x6c0) and omits DMTE4-7 (H&#x27;780-H&#x27;7E0), which exist on SH7750R/SH7751R (cpu_sh.c:447-448).  LOW today because nothing in the tree asserts any DMTE; it becomes MED when `sh4dmacintr` lands, and the loop is to be extended in that round || emulmkstempexit -- emul.c:600-603 calls exit(1) when mkstemp fails -- a host temporary-directory failure ends the process || arcpartlba -- OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:2730-2731 at db8b1a33 -- the ARC partition LBA is multiplied by 512 in signed int and overflows (arcbios.c:1010-1017; it defeats the #168 bound)</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th sc