t flag, nothing more.  REACHED BY (by reading, not measured): SCMD/PCTL give the guest control of the phase.  FIX SHAPE: keep the CPU running while KEEPING the helper&#x27;s early return (:170 / :236) -- the treatment #186 gave the XFR command at :507.  PROVENANCE: agy&#x27;s ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -&gt; GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s finding that the title carries one of nine `cpu-&gt;running = 0` assignments (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_agyflags/codex_aconf_agyflags.txt) -&gt; grok&#x27;s ruling, CONCEDE IN PART, three rows (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/grok/grok_mbstops.txt) -&gt; Astra&#x27;s confirmation (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_mbstops/codex_aconf_mbstops.txt: CONFIRMED WITH CHANGES (3) -- correct reachability explanations, qualify carrier/title scope, and label evidence as source-only; retain three HIGH rows).  Severity HIGH by the qhm88kstops grade (a guest-drivable stop of the emulated CPU).  Reachability established by source inspection at c29a5fd3; no runtime witness measured -- the round that takes this row owes the rung-3 attempt.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) by #558 on grok&#x27;s ruling (grok-4.7 xhigh, plan mode) and Astra&#x27;s confirmation of it (GPT-6 Astra, ultra); the chain is in the row&#x27;s note.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g