e, or the EXBF register stops the emulated CPU while mb89352_abort_on_unimplemented_stuff is fixed true — note: FILED BY #558 from queue passage 2616 at db8b1a33 (&#x27;#12 m88k CMMU / dev_mb89352 fatal errors&#x27;), which #555 gave ONE row (qhm88kstops, dev_mb89352.c:146).  SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :312 (len != 1: a halfword or word callback access), :533 (an SCMD WRITE outside {0x00, 0x20, 0x84, 0x8c, 0xc0} unless bit 0x10 rewrites it to BUS_REL -- an SCMD read does not execute this switch), and EXBF, register index 15: WRITE logging at :676 and READ logging at :683 converge on the ONE assignment at :690.  All gated by const bool mb89352_abort_on_unimplemented_stuff = true (:61), so live; the shared fixed-true policy is what groups them.  REACHED BY (by reading, not measured): those accesses from the guest&#x27;s register interface.  FIX SHAPE: the warning branch the flag already selects; clearing the flag leaves all five live unconditional DREG assignments (:146, :169, :176, :235, :242; :290 is dead) intact.  NOT mb89352halt&#x27;s stop: that dropped row&#x27;s record names the disk dispatcher&#x27;s CDB default: and the controller&#x27;s status-length guard, not :533.  PROVENANCE: agy&#x27;s ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -&gt; GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s finding that the title carries one of nine `cpu-&gt;running = 0` assignments (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_agyflags/codex_aconf_agyflags.txt) -&gt; grok&#x27;s ruling, CONCEDE IN PART, three rows (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/grok/grok_mbstops.txt) -&gt; Astra&#x27;s confirmation (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_mbstops/codex_aconf_mbstops.txt: CONFIRMED WITH CHANGES (3) -- correct reachability explanations, qualify carrier/title scope, and label evidence as source-only; retain three HIGH rows).  Severity HIGH by the qhm88kstops grade (a guest-drivable stop of the emulated CPU).  Reachability established by source inspection at c29a5fd3; no runtime witness measured -- the round that takes this row owes the rung-3 attempt.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) by #558 on grok&#x27;s ruling (grok-4.7 xhigh, plan mode) and Astra&#x27;s confirmation of it (GPT-6 Astra, ultra); the chain is in the row&#x27;s note.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">qhmbbufendstops</span><span class="ttl">An MB89352 data-register access at or past the end of the selected buffer, in a phase supported for the access direction, stops the emulated CPU</span><span class="tip">An MB89352 data-register access at or past the end of the selected buffer, in a phase supported for the access direction, stops the emulated CPU — note: FILED BY #558 from queue passage 2616 at db8b1a33 (&#x27;#12 m88k CMMU / dev_mb89352 fatal errors&#x27;), which #555 gave ONE row (qhm88kstops, dev_mb89352.c:146).  SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :176 (DREG read, transfer_bufpos &gt;= len against the selected DATAIN, STAT or MSGIN buffer -- read completion changes phase WITHOUT resetting the cursor, so a subsequent nonempty buffer can meet this guard, not only the original DATAIN buffer) and :242 (DREG write: reachable through empty or unprepared outgoing-buffer states; an exact fill runs completion and can change phase so a further write reaches :235 instead).  PREREQUISITES: a transfer object and a nonzero count, as for the phase guards (the count prerequisite applies to every DREG helper call; the :146 stop is the case with NO transfer object).  CARRIERS OF THE REST: b120 carries the unknown-CDB producer omission and its empty-status consequence; this row&#x27;s residual is every OTHER empty-buffer path and every nonempty-buffer case.  FIX SHAPE: keep the bounds protection and refuse the access or handle phase completion -- removing the guard exposes the indexed accesses at :180 / :246 -- a CONTROLLER fix; b120 remains the PRODUCER fix.  PROVENANCE: agy&#x27;s ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -&gt; GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s finding that the title carries one of nine `cpu-&gt;running = 0` assignments (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_agyflags/codex_aconf_agyflags.txt) -&gt; grok&#x27;s ruling, CONCEDE IN PART, three rows (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/grok/grok_mbstops.txt) -&gt; Astra&#x27;s confirmation (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_mbstops/codex_aconf_mbstops.txt: CONFIRMED WITH CHANGES (3) -- correct reachability explanations, qualify carrier/title scope, and label evidence as source-only; retain three HIGH rows).  Severity HIGH by the qhm88kstops grade (a guest-drivable stop of the emulated CPU).  Reachability established by source inspection at c29a5fd3; no runtime witness measured -- the round that takes this row owes the rung-3 attempt.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) by #558 on grok&#x27;s ruling (grok-4.7 xhigh, plan mode) and Astra&#x27;s confirmation of it (GPT-6 Astra, ultra); the chain is in the row&#x27;s note.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</