ree seats FILE, HIGH, own row (regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/astra/D_secondreadings/codex_adjD.txt, grok/D_secondreadings/grok_adjD.txt, fable5/fable5_adj_D_secondreadings_v2_FABLE.md).  Source: prescreen_audits5.md of_two/F9.  READ at HEAD by all three: of.c:1096-1101 (the NULL check and the exit), :1078 (the only writer, of_emul_init, called only from machine_macppc.c:99); ARM decode cpu_arm_instr.c:5034-5036 -&gt; X(openfirmware) :988-991; PowerPC decode cpu_ppc_instr.c:4400-4402 -&gt; X(openfirmware) :3956-3958.  A guest instruction therefore ends the emulator process on machines that never set up OpenFirmware.  Not covered by ofopenexit or ofpeerexit (other sites in the same file); Fable 5.1: may share one round with them.  A rung-3 ATTEMPT exists, made by claude-opus-4-8 in the Fable seat&#x27;s fallback run (so it is not a Fable ruling and owes review before it counts as the witness): regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/meas_D/witness_hostexit.py and .out, at HEAD e483d931 on the unmodified ARM test machine (the emulator prints `of_emul(): no of_data struct?&#x27; and the process exits 1), each with a benign-instruction liveness control that stays alive.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span>