 self_label; it fails nothing); the usage string prints only when the probe gets fewer than two arguments, which gate 13 never does; the split note is Grok 4.7&#x27;s (#565 F2).  Cosmetic: no gate, kill or score rests on any of the three.  A round touching the probe&#x27;s docstring -- `ppcprobescorestale&#x27;&#x27;s demotion is the next one -- can close it.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">ppc527residual</span><span class="ttl">#527&#x27;s five residuals, moved here from `ppcrldimimask` at its closure: the SH=63/MB=1 full-mask rldimi row, the wrapping stale-rS alias row, the Rc=1-only insertion skip, CENSUS_SHRINK and R_NOGUARD -- coverage debt and named measurements on regress/ppc_rlwimi_probe.py and ppc_rldimi_probe.py, none a floor breach</span><span class="tip">#527&#x27;s five residuals, moved here from `ppcrldimimask` at its closure: the SH=63/MB=1 full-mask rldimi row, the wrapping stale-rS alias row, the Rc=1-only insertion skip, CENSUS_SHRINK and R_NOGUARD -- coverage debt and named measurements on regress/ppc_rlwimi_probe.py and ppc_rldimi_probe.py, none a floor breach — witness: none — note: filed 2026-10-18 by #527&#x27;s closure-records commit.  Fable 5.1&#x27;s 2026-09-12 closing ruling (regress/artifacts/xscaleinten/fable_adjudication_20260912.md) graded each clause (e) or a named measurement, not owed before #527&#x27;s commit, and asked that they be FILED; the 2026-10-02 disposition (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/AGY_FLAGS_DISPOSITION.md, flags #10-#14) then made `ppcrldimimask` their carrier -- &#x27;the carrier owes its recorded work whenever its round runs&#x27;.  This row carries them now, so that row could close (GPT-6 Astra, #527&#x27;s closure check).  The five, specified in OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md under `ppcrldimimask` -- SHIPPED: (1) ADD a full-mask patterned rldimi row at SH=63, MB=1 from 0xDEADBEEFCAFEF00D, want 0xEF56DF77E57F7806 (costs a table 4 and pin 29 -&gt; 30); (2) an alias row at SH=40, MB=40 for a stale rS re-read on WRAPPING masks (codex&#x27;s arithmetic, not built); (3) an insertion skipped only when Rc=1 survives both probes (both CONTRACTs disclose it); (4) CENSUS_SHRINK -- one run of the fixed build with a shortened census, the literal pins&#x27; unique channel; (5) R_NOGUARD -- delete rlwimi&#x27;s `sh ?` guard, predicted 28/28, load-bearing for definedness since the fix narrowed tmp (Fable).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">ip30stallgreen</span><span class="ttl">ip30_abort_probe.py reads a load-stalled session as a run whose remaining accesses never happened: session() returns alive=True for a child its 12 s poll kills, holding only the transcript read before the poll -- so on V2_assigntick, xbit rev2&#x27;s session stalling with exactly one ISR announce captured leaves all 41 gate-14 checks green</span><span class="tip">ip30_abort_probe.py reads a load-stalled session as a run whose remaining accesses never happened: session() returns alive=True for a child its 12 s poll kills, holding only the transcript read before the poll -- so on V2_assigntick, xbit rev2&#x27;s session stalling with exactly one ISR announce captured leaves all 41 gate-14 checks green — witness: none — note: filed 2026-10-18 by #566 (GPT-6 Astra and Grok 4.7, pass 2 and F2).  A stall BEFORE a session&#x27;s access leaves its `alive&#x27; and `no&#x27; rows green -- the kill rows, `acc 30 rd&#x27;, `tick 49&#x27;, the read arms&#x27; `txt&#x27; rows -- and its `yes&#x27; row red (the write-arm and bit-50 tick sessions carry one); a count row that wants ONE announce (latch 1x, latch 28wr, latch 30wr, latch tick, xbit rev, xbit rev2) reads green whenever exactly one was captured, so V2_assigntick goes all-green when xbit rev2&#x27;s session stalls with one ISR announce captured and every other session passes.  The reap after the SIGKILL is a blocking waitpid and gate_arm.sh puts no timeout on the probe.  Repair shape: a per-session completion marker every row requires -- a probe change, owing a kill table.  Disclosed in the gate block&#x27;s comment.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">ip30abortresidual</span><span class="ttl">#531&#x27;s residuals, carried here from ip30abortkill for its close: V7_nocounter (delete `d-&gt;reg_0x20000 += 1000&#x27;: 32/32 in kill table 4) and the width axis V8_len4 (`&amp;&amp; len == 4&#x27; on the 0x10020 write guard: 33/33 in kill table 5), both disclosed coverage debt; and three questions #531 filed and never disposed of -- the announce string&#x27;s truth at the 0x10020/0x10028 write arms, the per-instance latch axis, fall-through after a non-exiting fatal().  None a floor breach</span><span class="tip">#531&#x27;s residuals, carried here from ip30abortkill for its close: V7_nocounter (delete `d-&gt;reg_0x20000 += 1000&#x27;: 32/32 in kill table 4) and the width axis V8_len4 (`&amp;&amp; len == 4&#x27; on the 0x10020 write guard: 33/33 in kill table 5), both disclosed coverage debt; and three questions #531 filed and never disposed of -- the announce string&#x27;s truth at the 0x10020/0x10028 write arms, the per-instance latch axis, fall-through after a non-exiting fatal().  None a floor breach — witness: none — note: filed 2026-10-18 with ip30abortkill&#x27;s closure records, so that row can close without dropping them.  (1) V7_nocounter -- the probe&#x27;s CONTRACT has it under MEASURED ESCAPES (MH_nocounter): the counter is UNCONDITIONAL, above the de-fatalised guard, so fix-independent (the fable5 ruling of 2026-09-18); measured on the 32-row instrument, not re-run at 33.  The shipped `acc 20000&#x27; row cannot see it by construction: its oracle accepts any readback - 0x1234 that is a non-negative multiple of 1000 (`_d20000 &gt;= 0&#x27;), so N = 0 passes -- table 4&#x27;s V7 log shows that row green (GLM 5.3 predicted the opposite at the closure check).  (2) V8_len4 -- under DOES NOT CATCH: the guarded body never tests len, so by the pcc2widthkills bound it is a single-operand marginal; cheap -- len takes at most four values and the probe already has guest_store64/guest_load64.  (1) and (2) are COVERAGE DEBT above the floor, FILED as the floor&#x27;s own rule says; not owed before ip30abortkill&#x27;s close.  Grok 4.7 dissented at the closure check: they need no carrier and stay disclosed in the CONTRACT (grok_close531.txt).  (3) three questions #531&#x27;s CHANGELOG block filed (`Also filed:&#x27;, under RECORDED, NOT RESOLVED) and regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/PRETABLE3.out lists the first two of -- the announce string&#x27;s TRUTH (`interrupt-status rewrite not implemented&#x27; is printed by the 0x10020 and 0x10028 write arms, which keep their stores; glm and kimi), the per-INSTANCE latch axis (N = 1 per device instance, the tree ships sgi_ip30_2, every row runs against one instance; kimi), and fall-through after a non-exiting fatal() (deepseek).  #531&#x27;s F13 ruling silenced the read arms and settled none of the three; this row does not claim them repaired, and they were on no ledger row (GPT-6 Astra, the closure check).  Owed when this row&#x27;s round runs: for (1) and (2), a row each or a recorded decision not to; for (3), an explicit disposition of each.  dev_sgi_ip30.c&#x27;s stale comment counts are #561&#x27;s held places 7-10, carried by heldrecedits; the load-stall green is ip30stallgreen.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">heldrecedits</span><span class="ttl">#560 and #561 HELD 30 ruled corrections on 2026-10-06 that no ledger row carries: 29 src/ comments (#560&#x27;s 12, #561&#x27;s 17; each owes est/ byte-identity and build-tree propagation) and #560&#x27;s `hrec extra&#x27; comment in regress/diff_ieee_store.c (:296-301) -- the bug file&#x27;s #560 and #561 sections end `Still owed&#x27;</span><span class="tip">#560 and #561 HELD 30 ruled corrections on 2026-10-06 that no ledger row carries: 29 src/ comments (#560&#x27;s 12, #561&#x27;s 17; each owes est/ byte-identity and build-tree propagation) and #560&#x27;s `hrec extra&#x27; comment in regress/diff_ieee_store.c (:296-301) -- the bug file&#x27;s #560 and #561 sections end `Still owed&#x27; — witness: none — note: filed 2026-10-18 with ip30abortkill&#x27;s closure records.  The lists are OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md&#x27;s `### #560&#x27; section (HELD (20)) and `### #561&#x27; section (HELD (17): every src/ comment, each with its ruled replacement under regress/artifacts/recordfix_20261002/adjudication_20261006/EDITS_561.json key `held&#x27;); #560&#x27;s rulings are its ADJ_FINAL.md and ADJ_HREC_FINAL.md.  This row carries the 30 of those 37 that no ledger row carried: the 29 src/ comments -- #560&#x27;s 12, dev_pcc2.c&#x27;s among them (held then because the peer session&#x27;s uncommitted work sits in that file), and #561&#x27;s 17 -- and #560&#x27;s `hrec extra&#x27; (diff_ieee_store.c:296-301).  #560&#x27;s other seven held sites (hrec 2, 9, 10, 19a-c, 20) are hrecordowed&#x27;s members hbundle_regress15:F7, hbundle_tools1:F5/F6 and hdiffieeestore:F6/F7, and stay there (GPT-6 Astra, the confirm).  Four of the 29 are #561&#x27;s places 7-10, dev_sgi_ip30.c&#x27;s stale comment counts, which ip30abortkill&#x27;s closure check first proposed to move onto ip30abortresidual -- a split of one held set (Grok 4.7).  The lists are as of 2026-10-06, and #565 has since corrected hrec 2&#x27;s claim, so the round reconciles each item against HEAD before applying it.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr c