r its wall (GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s confirm).  Census: regress/artifacts/fableheldform/design_20261018/CENSUS_wide.txt (by seat: kimi 129, agy 96, fable5 75, codex 75, opus5 37, minimax 33, grok 23, glm 17, deepseek 12; by month: 2026-08 132, 2026-09 301, 2026-10 64), a keyword net -- 497 MATCHES among entries counted as answers, which include actual non-answers and known false positives (genuine answers that quote the keywords); not a count of the class.  fableheldform fixed only its own slice (Fable&#x27;s walls since the owner&#x27;s 2026-10-17 hold, plus one of 2026-10-16).  Owed: (1) a STRUCTURAL check, forward-only from a cutoff, that reds a NEW entry recording a non-answer (NOT FIRED, SEAT FAILURE, walled, stalled) without a stage token -- keyword-based, so it must say so and carry negative controls; (2) an owner ruling on how a deliberately excluded seat is recorded: the non-answer token makes a narrowed-roster stage read short under section H&#x27;s nine-seat count, while an untokened note makes it read as answered; (3) the historical entries are corrected row by row when a round touches them, not swept.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td 