6) committed sgi_mte_decline_probe.py -- promptless -- and moved neither EXPECT_PTY_PROBES nor the grandfathered list, so the 2026-10-18 battery would have reddened gate 6 (instances before it: #500&#x27;s probe, and the 24 probes of the 2026-09 hygienecensus drift) — witness: none — note: filed 2026-10-18 by #567, which found it while re-deriving its own pins: tools/derive_hygiene_pins.sh reported the pty census 76 vs its pin 74 and the promptless census 44 vs 43, and refused --write while sgi_mte_decline_probe.py stood neither grandfathered nor prompt-detecting.  #567 grandfathered it on the 2026-09-19 precedent and wrote the pins.  The landing spot is STRUCTURAL: a precommit section that runs the deriver in report mode and refuses a commit whose tree leaves a census off its pin -- forward-only, controlled both ways (a pty probe added without its pin reds; with it, greens).  The design question it owes: the precommit sees the STAGED tree while the pin counts what lies in the WORKING tree (owner ruling 2026-09-23, &#x27;count all&#x27;), so the check must be defined against one of them.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span 