-   "state_note": "[2026-09-19 06:2x] #540 IN WORK (e8a2bc): fix + a 28-row detector; the re-table ran 22 of 22 legs as predicted (regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/killtable2_20260919/); pass 3 (the repair chain) in flight on panel_20260919_060901, fable5 last.    *** SEVERITY RAISED med -> HIGH 2026-09-17 on the grok seat's finding, which is EVIDENCED rather than asserted: the 'entire window dies' claim HOLDS for this nested address, the symptom is total window death PLUS a floodclass flood, and **every existing LCA probe and #530's own 352-row detector run with PTBR=0, so it is invisible to all of them**.  It is the FIRST of the three LCA rounds.  Fix is one flag on two calls (`CACHE_NONE | PHYSICAL', the house idiom) and does not disturb #530's packing. ***  *** THAT RAISE WAS REVERTED THE SAME DAY.  I claimed the downgrade had 'no recorded warrant anywhere'; IT HAS ONE, ten lines above the entry in OUTSTANDING_BUGS -- a three-premise analysis dated 2026-09-11.  My grep searched for the ROW ID and for 'was HIGH'; the rationale is a SHARED SECTION HEADER over three rows and contains neither, so a pattern that matched nothing returned a confident absence and I recorded it as fact.  *** AND IT IS THE EXACT ERROR THAT BLOCK WARNS ABOUT: its author wrote 'I filed this HIGH on a pass-1 seat's quoted sentence without the evidence under it', and I then raised it to HIGH on a seat's quoted sentence without the evidence under it. ***  WHAT SURVIVES: grok refuted premise (b) on the code (it is about K0SEG VAs, not 0x1d0000000; a coincidental valid PTE there aliases ISA onto RAM, WORSE than not_found).  **Premise (c) -- no in-tree LCA guest is shown to enable paging -- stands UNREFUTED, and severity turns on (c).**  MEDIUM stands; the FIX is still right. ***"
+   "state_note": "[2026-09-21 13:5x] #540 (e8a2bc): the fix and its records are COMMIT-READY and the round is held for the Fable adjudication, which is HELD by owner directive (the same hold the peer session recorded at 10:2x on 09-19).  Nothing else blocks it."
