-   "state_note": "crime_width_probe.py is the instrument behind today's #529 ctl0c discharge (202/204); lca_isalane_probe.py is the 352-row #530 detector and the file the lcaisaphys witness spec copies its helpers from.  A fresh clone has the measurements and not the instruments.  check_probe_wiring.py's domain() is `git ls-files' (COMMITTED-OR-STAGED, per its own docstring) while its GHOST message said 'regress/ has no such file' -- a wrong record that discredited a true finding; corrected the same day.  150 GHOST rows: 148 per-round artifact copies, exactly 2 top-level detectors.  *** CORRECTED SAME HOUR: the exposure is PROSPECTIVE, not present.  The COMMITTED gate_arm.sh has ZERO references to crime_width_probe (git show HEAD:regress/gate_arm.sh | grep -c) -- only the MODIFIED working copy invokes it at :1658.  A fresh clone today is consistent.  THE REAL FINDING IS A COMMIT-ORDERING CONSTRAINT: gate_arm.sh and crime_width_probe.py MUST be staged in the SAME commit, or the commit itself creates a battery invoking a missing file.  lca_isalane_probe.py is in no gate and carries no such constraint.  Neither probe has an EXPECT_ROWS identity row (floor clause (c)); both have a _DONE sentinel and a _RESULT= line.  I wrote 'a fresh clone has the measurements and not the instruments' from the working tree without asking git what HEAD contains.  *** RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-18, AND THE EXPOSURE IS WIDER THAN THE ROW SAID. ***  `git ls-files --error-unmatch' confirms BOTH detectors are untracked: regress/crime_width_probe.py (119,216 bytes) and regress/lca_isalane_probe.py (99,545 bytes) -- 214 KB of SHIPPED, MEASURED detector code that exists in no commit.  AND THE BROADER FIGURE: `git status --porcelain regress/' reports **149 untracked paths** under regress/, which now includes EVERY #531 artifact -- all three killtable dirs, all three PRETABLE blocks, the opus seat's preserved logs, and the frozen 18-row instrument.  A working-tree loss today destroys the two detectors AND the entire evidence base for #531's floor discharge.  *** NOT RESOLVED THIS CYCLE, AND THE REASON IS CONTENTION, NOT OVERSIGHT: *** the fix is a COMMIT (staging protects nothing), a commit owes its targeted gate, and a gate is CPU-heavy while an opus5 measuring seat is in flight.  Queued for the moment that seat lands.  Constraints carried: stage BY NAME, never `git add -A'; regress/*.bin (alpha_dummy.bin, arm_bfx_stub.bin) and regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py MUST NOT be staged; #529 and #530 commit SEPARATELY; LOCAL GIT ONLY -- DO NOT PUSH.  *** RESOLVED IN SUBSTANCE 2026-09-18: 150 GHOST paths STAGED BY NAME, and the ghost count went 150 -> 3 -> 0. ***  Both detectors (crime_width_probe.py 119,216 b; lca_isalane_probe.py 99,545 b) are now visible to `git ls-files'.  Staged with an explicit cross-check that NOTHING on the do-not-commit list was touched -- verified zero before and after (ppc_rldicl_probe.py, regress/*.bin, gdromdefault_461, disk.img, commit518, the tools/ carrier copies).  *** AND THE LAST THREE COULD NOT BE CLEARED BY STAGING OR BY COMMITTING, BECAUSE THEY WERE A CHECK THAT CANNOT PASS. ***  See `wiringshghost'.  STILL OWED: the COMMIT itself.  Staging makes the files visible to the checkers and re-enables the checks the untracked state had switched off, but it does NOT protect against working-tree loss -- only a commit does.  Blocked on the remaining hard gate failures and on #531's close (fable outstanding).",
+   "state_note": "crime_width_probe.py is the instrument behind today's #529 ctl0c discharge (202/204); lca_isalane_probe.py is the 352-row #530 detector and the file the lcaisaphys witness spec copies its helpers from.  A fresh clone has the measurements and not the instruments.  check_probe_wiring.py's domain() is `git ls-files' (COMMITTED-OR-STAGED, per its own docstring) while its GHOST message said 'regress/ has no such file' -- a wrong record that discredited a true finding; corrected the same day.  150 GHOST rows: 148 per-round artifact copies, exactly 2 top-level detectors.  *** CORRECTED SAME HOUR: the exposure is PROSPECTIVE, not present.  The COMMITTED gate_arm.sh has ZERO references to crime_width_probe (git show HEAD:regress/gate_arm.sh | grep -c) -- only the MODIFIED working copy invokes it at :1658.  A fresh clone today is consistent.  THE REAL FINDING IS A COMMIT-ORDERING CONSTRAINT: gate_arm.sh and crime_width_probe.py MUST be staged in the SAME commit, or the commit itself creates a battery invoking a missing file.  lca_isalane_probe.py is in no gate and carries no such constraint.  Neither probe has an EXPECT_ROWS identity row (floor clause (c)); both have a _DONE sentinel and a _RESULT= line.  I wrote 'a fresh clone has the measurements and not the instruments' from the working tree without asking git what HEAD contains.  *** RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-18, AND THE EXPOSURE IS WIDER THAN THE ROW SAID. ***  `git ls-files --error-unmatch' confirms BOTH detectors are untracked: regress/crime_width_probe.py (119,216 bytes) and regress/lca_isalane_probe.py (99,545 bytes) -- 214 KB of SHIPPED, MEASURED detector code that exists in no commit.  AND THE BROADER FIGURE: `git status --porcelain regress/' reports **149 untracked paths** under regress/, which now includes EVERY #531 artifact -- all three killtable dirs, all three PRETABLE blocks, the opus seat's preserved logs, and the frozen 18-row instrument.  A working-tree loss today destroys the two detectors AND the entire evidence base for #531's floor discharge.  *** NOT RESOLVED THIS CYCLE, AND THE REASON IS CONTENTION, NOT OVERSIGHT: *** the fix is a COMMIT (staging protects nothing), a commit owes its targeted gate, and a gate is CPU-heavy while an opus5 measuring seat is in flight.  Queued for the moment that seat lands.  Constraints carried: stage BY NAME, never `git add -A'; regress/*.bin (alpha_dummy.bin, arm_bfx_stub.bin) and regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py MUST NOT be staged; #529 and #530 commit SEPARATELY; LOCAL GIT ONLY -- DO NOT PUSH.  *** RESOLVED IN SUBSTANCE 2026-09-18: 150 GHOST paths STAGED BY NAME, and the ghost count went 150 -> 3 -> 0. ***  Both detectors (crime_width_probe.py 119,216 b; lca_isalane_probe.py 99,545 b) are now visible to `git ls-files'.  Staged with an explicit cross-check that NOTHING on the do-not-commit list was touched -- verified zero before and after (ppc_rldicl_probe.py, regress/*.bin, gdromdefault_461, disk.img, commit518, the tools/ carrier copies).  *** AND THE LAST THREE COULD NOT BE CLEARED BY STAGING OR BY COMMITTING, BECAUSE THEY WERE A CHECK THAT CANNOT PASS. ***  See `wiringshghost'.  STILL OWED: the COMMIT itself.  Staging makes the files visible to the checkers and re-enables the checks the untracked state had switched off, but it does NOT protect against working-tree loss -- only a commit does.  Blocked on the remaining hard gate failures and on #531's close (fable outstanding).  *** MEASURED AGAIN 2026-09-21 BY THE PEER SESSION AND RE-VERIFIED HERE INDEPENDENTLY: THE STAGED STATE DID NOT SURVIVE, AND THE HEADLINE ABOVE IS THEREFORE A WRONG RECORD. ***  `git ls-files --error-unmatch': regress/crime_width_probe.py UNTRACKED, regress/arm_msrmode_probe.py UNTRACKED, regress/lca_isalane_probe.py TRACKED.  So ONE of the two original detectors was resolved the only way that works -- a COMMIT (a11eaac) -- and the other was not.  `git log -- regress/crime_width_probe.py' returns NOTHING, so that file has never been in any commit; the peer believes their `git reset -q' of 2026-09-19 06:1x dropped the staged paths, and I cannot separate that from `never committed at all' -- recorded as UNSETTLED cause, same remedy either way.  THE ROW'S OWN LAST LINE WAS RIGHT AND ITS HEADLINE WAS NOT: `staging makes the files visible ... but it does NOT protect against working-tree loss -- only a commit does'.  A row whose headline says RESOLVED IN SUBSTANCE and whose tail says STILL OWED is read by its headline.  *** AND THE SCOPE IS TWO FILES, NOT 147: *** `git status --porcelain regress/' reports 147 untracked paths today, of which 145 are ARTIFACTS directories belonging to rounds in flight (56 crimewidthkill, 16 lcaisaphys, 8 alphavmkill, 8 wdcaltdigin, 6 ppcrlwhighhalf, 3 alphaifetchkill, ...).  EXACTLY TWO are probes.  NEITHER IS MINE TO STAGE: crime_width_probe.py belongs to #529, which my standing constraints forbid me to touch, and arm_msrmode_probe.py belongs to `armmsrmodekill', an open HIGH nobody has started.  They land with their own rounds' commits.  The row's TITLE is also half stale -- it names lca_isalane_probe.py, which is now tracked; the live pair is crime_width_probe.py and arm_msrmode_probe.py.  OWNER QUESTION OPEN from both sessions: commit them, exclude them from the hygiene census, or leave the census counting them.  *** AND THE OBJECT DB SETTLES THE CAUSE, 2026-09-21 -- raised by the peer session, RE-MEASURED HERE, and it produced a fact neither of us had. ***  Staging writes a blob that a reset does not remove, so `git fsck --unreachable' is the witness: **18 unreachable blobs whose first line names crime_width_probe.py** (the peer counted 13 on a narrower pattern), with loose-object mtimes clustering at 2026-09-19 03:43:07 and one at 09-14 -- so that file WAS staged, repeatedly.  The peer's `git reset -q' ran ~06:1x the same morning, just before 7836071, and they record the loss as theirs with the honest caveat that a later reset by anyone would look identical.  **arm_msrmode